# Styles & markup

Plain CSS in `css/style.css` — no framework or preprocessor.

## BEM

Use `block__element--modifier`:

```html
<span class="row__eta row__eta--none"></span>
<div class="map-stage__map" id="focus-map"></div>
<div class="add-flow__input" id="add-route-input"></div>
```

## Theming

- Design tokens as CSS custom properties on `:root` and `[data-theme="dark"]`
- Toggle theme via `data-theme` on `<html>`
- Do not hardcode colors in CSS when a `--token` exists
- Map route colors are the exception (`ROUTE_COLORS` in `map.js`)
- Dark glass top-left highlight stays quiet (`--focus-glass-highlight` / `--glass-sheen` ~0.02–0.03); avoid a bright white sheen on the sheet and rows
- `.map-tiles--osm` applies the dark-theme filter only to OpenStreetMap base tiles. Keep route overlays, markers, and attribution unfiltered; CARTO uses native light/dark tiles.

## Mobile & a11y

- `viewport-fit=cover` for notched devices
- Touch-friendly targets; `aria-live="polite"` on dynamic sections (`#cards`)
- `role="button"` + keyboard (`Enter`/`Space`) for interactive rows
- `aria-label` / `aria-pressed` on each theme-toggle sun/moon button (no visual selected chrome)
- `aria-label` on floating `nav-dock` (above watch-sheet) and on `theme-toggle` group (map top-right)

## New UI

Add styles to `style.css` following existing glass/row/focus patterns. Keep light and dark variants in sync.

Notable blocks: `map-stage` (full-bleed Leaflet background), `watch-sheet` (bottom-half liquid-glass watchlist panel; uses `--watch-sheet-glass` for higher map transparency; equal `0.75rem` inset on left/right/bottom — ignores `safe-area-inset-bottom`; `--radius-watch-sheet` (`2.875rem`); scrollable `#cards` with scroll-aware `mask-image` edge fade via CSS scroll-driven animations — `--watch-sheet-scroll-fade` depth, `--scroll-fade-reveal` range; static dual-edge fallback when unsupported; `watch-sheet__status` spans the sheet top as plain overlay text — height `--watch-sheet-status-space`, no tint/blur frost), `row` / `row__slide` / `row__delete` (iOS-style swipe-to-delete), `add-anchor` (fixed stack above the sheet: `#add-flow` liquid-glass panel + `#add-menu` choice bubbles + circular **+**), `add-menu-backdrop` (full-screen blur when **+** menu open), `add-menu__choice` (glass pill buttons side-by-side: Find nearby / Enter manually), `add-flow` (route typeahead, direction chips, stop route list `.add-flow__route-list`; suggestions outside `#add-flow` for map backdrop blur), `add-pick-hint` (fixed top-center glass pill during map-pick), `focus-marker__add-pick-bar` / `focus-marker__add-pick-confirm` (route-first map pick only), `add-toast` (success feedback above the anchor), `nav-dock` (wraps **+** only; `--nav-add-size` `2.375rem`; `z-index` above menu bubbles), `nav-dock__add--clear` (+ → × when menu, add-flow, or multi-focus), `theme-toggle` (vertical sun/moon stack, map top-right under safe-area). Focus selection highlights only `.row--focused`, not the watch-sheet chrome. `#cards` scrolls without a visible scrollbar. `body.add-flow-active` and `body.add-menu-open` dim/disable interaction behind the add UI. Icons: `favicon.svg` / `favicon-32.png` / `apple-touch-icon.png` — blue bus (route color A) on `#eef1f6`.

Active segment nerve pulse (`js/pulse.js`): Leaflet SVG `.focus-route-pulse-track` (pearl fiber via `--focus-pulse-fiber`, weight 6, full current leg) + `.focus-route-pulse-comet` (uniform rounded dashes via `--focus-pulse-spark`, light drop-shadow, flowing across the remaining bus-to-next-stop section); traveling `strokeDashoffset` via rAF (`updateActiveSegmentMotion`), not CSS keyframes; `.focus-route-pulse-layer--visible` / `--exiting` for appearance/handoff fade; stationary stream when `prefers-reduced-motion`. Bus marker: `.focus-marker--bus` / `__bus` / `__bus-body` with route-color gradients (`--focus-bus` … `--focus-bus-f`); `.focus-marker--bus-b` … `--bus-f` variants. You marker: `.focus-marker--you` / `__you` / `__you-dot` / `__pulse` (36×36 icon, ~15px dot). Boarding stop name bubble: `.focus-marker__stop-label` (+ `__stop-label-text` / `__stop-label-sub`) on `.focus-marker--stop-labeled`; comma splits name onto `__stop-label-sub`; pin accent via `--stop-label-accent` (label itself has no color bar or caret).

Dash pattern: all rounded dashes have the same current length and gap. Individual geometric lengths shorten from 18 px at ≥300 m remaining to 3 px at ≤20 m; visible gaps tighten from 10 px to 3 px across that range. Scale lengths and gaps with zoom, keeping a visible gap of at least 1.5 px. Stroke width stays 3.5 px; round caps add that width to each painted dash length, so include caps when bounding the stream and deriving center spacing. Use an even SVG dash/gap list and a final gap beyond the path plus cap/spacing allowance. Motion stays at a steady pixel speed; preserve phase within one spacing through length/gap updates, style changes, and full ETA overlay repaints so dashes enter/exit naturally without a whole-stream wrap or opacity pulse. Retain pulse layers for unchanged active legs, clearing dropped/unavailable streams; a new physical leg resets phase. Keep dashes and their caps inside the remaining bus → next-stop section. Both pulse polylines use `noClip: true`; actual map zoom invalidates path measurements independently of the clamped visual scale. Reduced motion leaves the same stream stationary. Keep the existing pearl colors, glow, appearance/handoff fades, and physical leg bounds.

Swipe-to-delete: `.row__actions` / `.row__delete` sit behind `.row__slide`. At rest `.row__slide` matches main row chrome (no transform, so `backdrop-filter` glass looks the same); transform only while swiping/open. `.row` is `overflow: visible` at rest so the focused ring/glow isn’t clipped; `overflow: hidden` only while `.row--swiping` / `.row--swipe-open`. Delete squircle fades via `--row-swipe-progress`. Far/loading opacity on `.row` like main. Corner radii: watch-sheet `--radius-watch-sheet` (`2.875rem`); inner cards `--radius-inner` (`0.875rem`); text inputs `--radius-input` (`0.75rem`); delete `--radius-row-delete` (`0.75rem`); add-flow panel `--radius-add-flow` (`1.375rem`); theme stack `1rem`.

Map chrome: no zoom control on the main map (pinch/scroll still work); vertical `theme-toggle` sun/moon stack sits top-right; attribution sits above the sheet via bottom margin. Provider credits must remain visible: wrap attribution text on narrow screens instead of truncating with ellipsis.

## When shipping UI changes

Update this file if you add a new BEM block, theme token, or a11y pattern. Also update `docs/PRD.md` per [workflow.mdc](workflow.mdc) — same turn, no prompt needed.
